{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"515acda8-b22f-43be-bfea-2679da0a4179","status":"SUCCESS","response":"## ANSWER.md Created\n\nI have updated **`bot.py`** to use two `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` segments:\n\n* **Static block** – the unchanged `INSTRUCTIONS`.\n* **Dynamic block** – the per‑athlete context (`athlete_context(a, today)`).\n\nThe new `build_system` now returns these two blocks separately, ensuring that a `save_fact` write only invalidates the volatile tail while the static instructions remain cached.\n\nThe **ANSWER.md** file in the artifact directory contains a concise description of the changes made and lists the relevant parts of the colleague’s note that were applied.  \n\nYou can review the detailed diff and explanation there.\n","duration_seconds":32.812256,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":13374,"output_tokens":2177,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":102912,"total_tokens":15551}}}
